! Mining software repository with Pharo

Nicolas Hlad  (nicolas.hlad@berger-levrault.com)

""Abstract:""
Git platforms like GitLab, GitHub, and Bitbucket offer valuable insights into team dynamics and project workflows. 
In this regard, the field of Mining Software Repositories (MSR) focuses on techniques and tools to extract and analyze this data.

This presentation introduces GitProjectHealth (GPH), a framework to interact with Git platforms and analyze them. 
We built GPH leveraging the Moose metamodel platform to create an extensible metamodel of a Git platform. 
Furthermore, we utilize the metamodel extension mechanism to connect Git platforms and other social platform models, such as Jira (ticket management).

This talk will cover three aspects of GPH: first, its ability to analyze Git repositories; second, 
its built-in metrics; and finally, its metamodel connection demonstrated with Jira. 

""Bio:""
Nicolas Hlad is a PhD computer scientist at Berger-Levrault, France. He completed his PhD in 2022, focusing on software product lines. 
Since then, he has been working on software static analysis using metamodel technology built in Pharo, and on how Generative Artificial 
Intelligence (GenAI), such as Large Language Models (LLMs), can impact the work of developers. Recently, he has used MSR as a means to 
analyze developers' activity when they benefit from GenAI LLM tools in their workflow.
